other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Romcol/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-06-26T09:27:21Z","updated_at":"2019-06-26T09:27:48Z","body":"Hi, thank you for fixing the bug !!\r\n\r\nI don't quite get what native validation has to do with that though :confused: \r\n\r\nRegarding my problematic, we actually need to link onChange to both input, as the form could be filled in reverse order (quite tricky right :laughing:) https://codesandbox.io/s/react-hook-form-seterror-fj6ds?fontsize=14.\r\n\r\nAlso, we want to display errors only after the form has been submitted, not while the confirm field is being completed, as it will display error to quickly. It would be better if it could be the default behavior (as for other fields). But I guess we can use `formState.submitCount > 0` to check if the form has ever been submitted.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, regarding the use of the `validate` rule, it doesn't quite work as expected (see https://codesandbox.io/s/react-hook-form-seterror-vbrup). It keeps displaying errors even when the inputs are correct and doesn't listen to input change.\r\n\r\nIt would be better if fields comparison would be supported out of the box and without using `setError`. But not sure it would not overwhelm the library.\r\n\r\nAnyways, thank you very much for the library and for processing my bug request!\r\n\r\nHave a good day!\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react-hook-form/react-hook-form/issues/comments/505796702/react